Finally won my first game without ever having to use the copy-the-backup
method.  The last couple of times, I only restored from a backup copy to
get around really stoopid goofs on my part -- the real me hasn't yet
acquired sleep resistance.  ("OK, I'll just quaff that potion of
paralysis at the minotaur... AUGH!")

When you read a scroll of charging, it lists all the items in your pack
as chargeable:  what effect does it have on items other than lamps or
wands?  Does it maybe increase the + value on rings, remove curses,
enchant weapons or armour?

Don't ever wish for an amulet of lifesaving (sp!).

Can you wish for a "blessed magic marker (1000)" or "wand of death
(50)"?

I was considering praying over and over again on level 1 or in the
endgame, trying to lose levels until I was level 1 with 15 hitpoints
again.  But I wasn't sure if maybe I'd be struck dead, and I DID want to
finish the game!  (96 HP, 63147 turns, and 11 dexterity at the end)

More interesting messages I've seen recently:

- "Spot drowns", when the floor underneath him became a pool.  I'd like
to see unfriendly monsters drown once in a while.

- "It whispers something to the thin air", when the & in the middle of
hell was a peaceful Geryon, peaceful Dispater, etc. and I tunneled
through wearing a ring of conflict.  Followed by "Geryon gets angry" and
some combat.  Why bother to make 'em peaceful?

- "This tastes like furniture polish!", quaffed a potion of booze while
hallucinating.

If you prevent the wizard from following you, you still get a visit from
a platoon of pets on level 1, and "vaguely nervous" feelings.  I
finished the game before finding out if the nervousness would pan out.

Unfair death:  quaffing from a fountain summoned a water demon (OK) and
a balrog (highly not OK!).

Stupid death on 1st turn:  "the book explodes in your face... you die...
(Killed by an exploding rune)".

My choice of what to wish for as a wimpy tourist:  gauntlets of power.
The extra carrying capacity and damage are just too crucial for someone
with 13 strength.  (Of course, it helps if you aren't wielding a cursed
weapon!!!)
